WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
- What could we expect from Season Two

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:02.840
from Saved by the Bell?

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.673
- I mean...

00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:04.506
- Which, did you watch?

00:00:04.506 --> 00:00:05.339
I watched Saved by the Bell,

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:06.172
and I'm a lot older than you, so.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.005
- Yeah, no.

00:00:07.005 --> 00:00:09.840
I - I wasn't, you know, I wasn't around

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.234
- I don't think alive or maybe...

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.090
- (indistinct).

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.820
I don't even think I was a thought.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.610
Well, I definitely wasn't a thought.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.200
I kind of just was a surprise, there.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.545
But that's a story for a different time.

00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:19.378
But no, I mean,

00:00:19.378 --> 00:00:22.480
the show is like a satirical
take on the original,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.890
which you've watched,

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.330
and it's sort of like a self-aware,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.130
version of the show that we all love.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.320
And season two is just
like a whole another level.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.153
I mean, we kind of have

00:00:32.153 --> 00:00:35.340
like this like weird mystery
element, which is very fun,

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.173
- Ooh OK

00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:38.150
- Like a little story to follow this year,

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:38.983
which is exciting.

00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:42.440
And then just getting to see
like all the OGs coming back.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.890
Lark Voorhies, who kills
it, and like everyone else,

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:46.723
which is awesome.

00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:47.556
So, think it will be fun

00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:49.110
- [Kelly] so wait, did you
watch any of the reruns?

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.070
Cause I just have a question.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.909
It's a very serious Saved
by the Bell question.

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:54.701
Are you more Zack Morris or AC Slater?

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.300
- I'm such a Zack Morris.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.278
- [Kelly] Okay, Zack Morris.

00:00:57.278 --> 00:00:58.530
- Are you kidding me?
- [Kelly] Okay, okay, okay.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.198
- Yeah, literally, Mario can like shut up.

00:01:00.198 --> 00:01:01.031
Just kidding.

00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:02.420
- Yeah, I loved

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.980
I loved both, but I was fascinated

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.990
that he always came out
in the wrestling uniform.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:07.823
AC slater

00:01:07.823 --> 00:01:08.656
- Zack Morris is beautiful

00:01:08.656 --> 00:01:09.790
- And I was like, OK AC
Slater in your spandex.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.204
- He's like the funny

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.850
(audience claps and cheers)

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.640
Here's the annoying thing about him.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.650
He still looks like Mario Lopez

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:18.500
still looks like that.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.993
What fountain has he found?

00:01:19.993 --> 00:01:20.826
I don't know

00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:21.980
- Mario is bionic

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.015
- It's crazy and Rude.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:26.110
So wait, you're a producer on this show,

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.100
which is awesome.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.110
So as a trans person,

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.910
like how has that helped with
telling authentic stories?

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.540
- Yeah, I mean, well,

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.070
and so like when the
show was brought to me,

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:39.010
it was like, obviously
very exciting opportunity,

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.360
but I felt that it was like
super important that if it was

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.800
gonna like step away from the school

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.150
and then tell this story in like the most

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.110
authentic way possible,

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.040
that the only way I could do
that is obviously, you know,

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.900
have some sort of
representation on both sides of

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.280
the camera, not just in front of it.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.320
And that producer role,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.730
I feel like allows us to tell
more of an authentic story

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.218
because there wasn't any
trans representation among,

00:02:01.218 --> 00:02:02.550
the producers.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.383
And I feel like because of it,

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.850
it's more entertaining
and it's more interesting

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:06.794
and it's more, like I said, authentic.

00:02:06.794 --> 00:02:07.627
- It's more diverse, yeah.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.460
- It's inspiring

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.293
- Thank you.

00:02:09.293 --> 00:02:10.126
- So inspiring

00:02:10.126 --> 00:02:10.959
It's important.

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:14.670
It's important that we don't
only just, diversify our cast,

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.700
but also the people telling the stories,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.780
which is awesome that I get to do it.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.613
(Audience Clapping)

00:02:19.613 --> 00:02:20.707
- I think it's so cool

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:21.850
- Do you have a desire to do behind

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.306
the scenes as well as on camera?

00:02:23.306 --> 00:02:24.139
- Yeah.

00:02:24.139 --> 00:02:24.972
- Yes definitely I'm-

00:02:24.972 --> 00:02:25.805
- She's like like boom, all the way.

00:02:25.805 --> 00:02:27.585
- Yeah I'll take your boom any day

00:02:27.585 --> 00:02:28.640
( giggling over )

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.960
- Um I'm a producer and Emily
too, which is really exciting.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:31.793
- So cool.

00:02:31.793 --> 00:02:34.140
- I didn't that that's something
you really want to pursue.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.070
- Yes.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.250
I love all aspects of the industry

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.989
and I've always wanted to create
stories from the ground up

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:41.822
- Yeah

00:02:41.822 --> 00:02:42.655
- And be involved in all

00:02:42.655 --> 00:02:43.488
aspects.

00:02:43.488 --> 00:02:44.540
- Even when I wasn't asked to be,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.900
I would always try to
be involved in some way

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.733
- Yeah I love that

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:49.410
Now I just love having the
title that allows me to feel

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.820
like I actually can.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.020
But, I feel like with season two,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.980
having had the experiences in season one

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.350
of being able to give,

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.610
be given the gift of critical
and creative criticism

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.190
and taking that and going, okay,

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.670
what can we do to be better,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.582
to do better?

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:04.415
[Kelly] Right.

00:03:04.415 --> 00:03:06.410
- We made it a really big point

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.210
to also diversify in it

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.691
and include more in front of the camera

00:03:09.691 --> 00:03:10.740
[Kelly] Which Is Important

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.530
as well as behind with,
our crew and the creators

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.390
and the storytellers.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.760
So, I really do think it's
like you said to, to say again,

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.101
like it's so important to have diversity

00:03:21.101 --> 00:03:22.221
and inclusion be a part of--

00:03:22.221 --> 00:03:23.390
- On our friends

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.893
- [Kelly] Representation, yeah absolutely

00:03:24.893 --> 00:03:25.726
(clapping)

00:03:25.726 --> 00:03:26.870
- [Josie] And by the way,
you know, it's so funny.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.640
I,it just, just came to my head.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.670
I didn't even think of it before,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:30.569
when they asked if we know each other,

00:03:30.569 --> 00:03:33.790
we don't know each other,
but one of your writers,

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.191
like taught a class of mine in college

00:03:36.191 --> 00:03:37.024
- Oh really?

00:03:37.024 --> 00:03:37.857
- Her name is Robin

00:03:37.857 --> 00:03:38.690
- Oh yeah!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.977
- [Josie] Yeah like Robin,
fully taught like in COVID.

00:03:40.977 --> 00:03:41.810
- So cool.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:42.643
- [Josie] Isn't that so random?

00:03:42.643 --> 00:03:43.570
- I know Robin too. That's so cool

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.522
that we all know Robin I know Robin too.

00:03:45.522 --> 00:03:46.480
I'm just kidding.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.313
(overlapping).

00:03:47.313 --> 00:03:48.577
- It's a small world.

00:03:48.577 --> 00:03:49.530
Here's the best.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.830
- Part though,I love about this.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.730
What just happened is like we
do like a panel show, right?

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.390
And like you think people
don't know each other,

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.280
but it's such a small world.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.870
Not even just like celebrities,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.270
like there'll be a
non-celebrity be like, oh yeah,

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.290
they worked with our organization.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.191
It's the craziest coolest thing.

00:04:01.191 --> 00:04:03.646
And that's what we love
about the panel here is that

00:04:03.646 --> 00:04:04.910
that happens.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.100
- I'm going to start
parking in your spot now.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.347
(audience claps and cheers)

00:04:10.347 --> 00:04:12.210
Anyone is welcomed to
mine if I'm not in it.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.300
- You an park in mine
if your down to hike,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.470
it's like running.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.625
- Here's why they probably
gave me that spot too not

00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:19.810
because I'm like famous or
that's just cause they were like,

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:22.560
she drives a huge truck and
there's no where to put it.

